    "futa (lid)",
    "kagi (lock: unlock it)"
   ],
   "flags": [],
   "use": "For opening a door yourself or asking someone to: doa akete (open the door), often with kureru when your hands are full. Casual speech drops o; a door that is open is doa aiteru.",
   "notes": "On the intercom, hai, ima akemasu ne (I'll let you in now) is a common reply when buzzing someone through the entrance; at your own front door it's usually hai, ima ikimasu.",
   "example": {
    "romaji": "gomen, doa akete kureru?",
    "ja": "ごめん、ドア開けてくれる？",
    "english": "Sorry, can you open the door for me?"
   },
   "examplePolite": {
    "romaji": "sumimasen, doa o akete moraemasu ka?",
    "ja": "すみません、ドアを開けてもらえますか？",
    "english": "Excuse me, could you open the door?"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "c-doa-o-shimeru",
   "romaji": "doa o shimeru",
